% Goal

Maintain the brownfield DJ brain workflow in brain/pick_candidates.py,
brain/mix_directives.py, brain/playlist_editor.py and brain/web/playlist.html.
Use the established provider registry for curation and notes; simplify the
mix builder without rewriting its musical planning or deterministic execution.

% Interface

run_pick(*, engine, brief, count=20, view_path, id_map_path, pool="new") -> list[dict].
PlaylistApp.ask_brain(brief, engine, count, pool="new") -> background job status.
Existing /api/brain, /api/brain/ask, /api/brain/apply, /api/directives and
/api/mix/build payloads remain compatible for provider-based requests.

<vocabulary>
duplicate: a candidate ID already accepted earlier in the same model response;
only its first occurrence is kept.
</vocabulary>

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): Curation and DJ-note interpretation use only brain.llm_providers;
reject nemoclaw, h-agent, generic and both with a clear retired-engine reason.
R2 (MUST NOT): Start Docker, NemoClaw, a desktop agent, web agent or GUI
bridge for curation, notes or model review.
R3 (MUST): Preserve New music's latest-scan scope and Whole library's keyword
prefilter; expose only synthetic candidate IDs to the model. Resolve IDs locally,
ignore unknown/duplicate IDs, and cap accepted picks to the requested count.
R4 (MUST NOT): Asking adds songs, finalizes a set, writes DJ notes or starts
playback. Picks and notes remain previews requiring the existing explicit action.
R5 (MUST): The GUI fills curation and mix provider choices from /api/providers,
disables unavailable providers and model-required actions when none is available,
and provides an explicit refresh for keys or a newly started local server.
R6 (MUST): The mix panel has one provider selector shared by Build and note
interpretation. Optimizer-only remains available, disables note interpretation,
and never sends a retired or unknown provider. Build consumes the brief once
through the established optimizer/review/choreography pipeline.
R7 (MUST): Preserve mix profiles, experimental-format accessibility under an
Advanced disclosure, candidate playback order, per-blend backbeat labels,
dry run warnings, analysis logs and separate Start mix confirmation. Idle polling
must not reset the user's profile, provider or transition-format choice.
R8 (MUST NOT): Claim a pleasant mix is proven by a dry run, or suggest that
unsupported same-song handoffs, harmonic count-1 detection, sustained 3-deck
support or measured sample pitch recovery are automatic features. Preserve
explicit authored performance plans rather than replacing them with Generic Build.
R9 (MUST): Build preserves the existing hard rules: effective DJ notes, source
exclusions, verse safety, phrase cues, stem layering, backbeat alignment, tempo/key
compatibility, gentle fades, exact-once track integrity and model-failure fallback.
</contract_rules>

% Verification

Synthetic fixtures exercise every provider through candidate picking and note
preview, retired-engine rejection before a worker starts, scope and count limits,
H API auth/model and .env refresh without leaking credentials, browser selection
retention, unavailable-provider handling, one shared model selection, and the
existing optimizer/notes/gentle-fader/source-boundary/performance tests.
